C. Is the dictionary 'unit cell <-> consecutive pair <-> triangular number <-> cycle' special to 3x+1?
   For q x + 1: unit cells |2^k - q^s| = 1 (k <= 400, s <= 250), every parity word of the cell is an integer cycle.
====================================================================================================
  3x+1: cell (1,0)  2^k - q^s = +1   pair (1,2)   T_1 = 1   periodic points of the cell: [0]  (all integral: True)
  3x+1: cell (1,1)  2^k - q^s = -1   pair (2,3)   T_2 = 3   periodic points of the cell: [-1]  (all integral: True)
  3x+1: cell (2,1)  2^k - q^s = +1   pair (3,4)   T_3 = 6   periodic points of the cell: [1, 2]  (all integral: True)
  3x+1: cell (3,2)  2^k - q^s = -1   pair (8,9)   T_8 = 36   periodic points of the cell: [-10, -7, -5]  (all integral: True)
  5x+1: cell (1,0)  2^k - q^s = +1   pair (1,2)   T_1 = 1   periodic points of the cell: [0]  (all integral: True)
  5x+1: cell (2,1)  2^k - q^s = -1   pair (4,5)   T_4 = 10   periodic points of the cell: [-2, -1]  (all integral: True)
  7x+1: cell (1,0)  2^k - q^s = +1   pair (1,2)   T_1 = 1   periodic points of the cell: [0]  (all integral: True)
  7x+1: cell (3,1)  2^k - q^s = +1   pair (7,8)   T_7 = 28   periodic points of the cell: [1, 2, 4]  (all integral: True)
  9x+1: cell (1,0)  2^k - q^s = +1   pair (1,2)   T_1 = 1   periodic points of the cell: [0]  (all integral: True)
  9x+1: cell (3,1)  2^k - q^s = -1   pair (8,9)   T_8 = 36   periodic points of the cell: [-4, -2, -1]  (all integral: True)
  15x+1: cell (1,0)  2^k - q^s = +1   pair (1,2)   T_1 = 1   periodic points of the cell: [0]  (all integral: True)
  15x+1: cell (4,1)  2^k - q^s = +1   pair (15,16)   T_15 = 120   periodic points of the cell: [1, 2, 4, 8]  (all integral: True)
  17x+1: cell (1,0)  2^k - q^s = +1   pair (1,2)   T_1 = 1   periodic points of the cell: [0]  (all integral: True)
  17x+1: cell (4,1)  2^k - q^s = -1   pair (16,17)   T_16 = 136   periodic points of the cell: [-8, -4, -2, -1]  (all integral: True)
  -> the dictionary exists for every q; the pair (8,9) is a unit cell twice: (3,2) for 3x+1 and (3,1) for 9x+1,
     both times with T_8 = 36 and a NEGATIVE cycle.  It is Catalan's pair, not a Collatz phenomenon.
  cell (11,7), 2^11 - 3^7 = -139: 330 words, integral periodic points: [-136, -91, -82, -68, -61, -55, -41, -37, -34, -25, -17]

